      { question: "What is the top trust tax rate in 2026?", answer: "37%, which a non-grantor trust reaches once its taxable income passes $16,000 for the year. A 3.8% Net Investment Income Tax can stack on top of that for undistributed investment income, producing a combined federal rate near 40.8%." },
      { question: "Do all trusts pay tax at the compressed trust brackets?", answer: "No. Only a non-grantor trust that keeps income pays tax at those compressed brackets. A grantor trust's income passes through to the person who created it and gets taxed at their individual rate instead." },
